{
  "//": "Copy to mods.local.json (gitignored). scenarioRoots lists, per mod id, the scenario folders of THAT mod's installation. A map found there is that mod's map, with no guessing; maps from the plain SCENARIO_ROOTS and uploaded maps are matched to a mod by the ids they reference. The mod ids are the ones build_mod.py registered in <ASSETS_DIR>/mods/index.json. The MOD_SCENARIO_ROOTS environment variable (modId=path;modId=path) wins over this file. gameRoots names each mod's game folder (the one with Globals, Imgs, Interf, Scripts) for the tests that read every table and archive of every mod (test-helpers/modRoots.ts); the D2_MOD_ROOTS environment variable (modId=path;modId=path) wins over it; tools/asset-pipeline/derive_mod.py finds a parent's install there too. closedMods lists mods that must not be shared (a closed beta): derive_mod.py refuses to derive from them without --allow-closed-parent, and tools/asset-pipeline/store_upload.py uploads them (and mods derived from them) without their install tables (the tables/*.dbf and capital.dat entries of mod.json, and the blobs only those name), so the PC that uploads must list them here.",
  "closedMods": ["some-closed-beta"],
  "gameRoots": {
    "some-mod": "D:/Games/Some Mod",
    "another-mod": "D:/Games/Another Mod/Game"
  },
  "scenarioRoots": {
    "some-mod": ["D:/Games/Some Mod/Exports", "D:/Games/Some Mod/Campaign"],
    "another-mod": ["D:/Games/Another Mod/Exports"]
  }
}
